  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/... \nForecast attention turns away from monsoon storm potential and\nback toward the extreme heat conditions starting Tuesday. The\nsubtropical high center will continue to shift westward into our\nregion into the middle part of the week with the center likely\nsettling somewhere over southern Arizona from Wednesday through at\nleast Friday or Saturday. Forecast H5 heights are also shown to\nreach 594-597dm for the latter half of the week which places it\njust shy of climatological records for late August. NBM\ntemperature guidance remains quite consistent showing highs rising\ninto a 112-116 degree range for the latter half of this week as\nconditions dry out. Daily temperature records in Phoenix will \ncontinue to be in jeopardy through the entire week, but are likely\nto fall short in Yuma and El Centro. Once the high center moves\noverhead by Wednesday, rain chances will essentially go to 5% or\nless. As of now, conditions for any monsoon storm activity do not\nlook good through next weekend.",
